From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yclu4 <yclu4@nuvoton.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] state-propose: skip no-buffer views instead of aborting
 PLANES_ONLY

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BSP-specific: GC520 2D/direct-KMS-scanout hack, not upstreamable as-is]

Re-diffed against Weston 13.0.1 (was written and hand-tested against
10.0.5 for Buildroot). Only carries forward one of that patch's two
fixes - see rationale below.

Fix carried forward - skip no-buffer views instead of aborting PLANES_ONLY
kiosk-shell creates a solid-colour background surface with no wl_buffer
(weston_solid_color_surface). drm_output_propose_state() sets
force_renderer=true for any view with !weston_view_has_valid_buffer(),
and in PLANES_ONLY mode renderer_ok is false, so 'if (!ps &&
!renderer_ok) goto err_region;' aborts the entire state proposal for
the whole output. A no-buffer view is invisible and contributes no
pixels; skip it with continue (matching the existing totally_occluded
handling immediately above) so real client surfaces can still be
promoted to hardware planes. This bug is unchanged between 10.0.5 and
13.0.1.

Fix dropped (superseded by upstream refactor) - the original patch's
second fix worked around drm_output_try_view_on_plane()'s overlay-vs-
primary guard (view_matches_entire_output && !scanout_has_view_assigned)
aborting the *entire* PLANES_ONLY proposal via 'availability =
NO_PLANES_ACCEPTED; goto out;' when two fullscreen clients were both
present. In 13.0.1 this same guard has been refactored to a plain
'continue' that only skips the overlay *candidate* for the current
view, while the PRIMARY/scanout plane candidate for that same view
(and the overlay candidate for the next view once scanout is taken) are
still considered - i.e. upstream already fixed the dual-fullscreen-
client case as a side effect of the per-view candidate-list rework.
Re-applying the old fix on top of this would be redundant.
---
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c
@@ -747,9 +747,23 @@
 		}
 
 		if (!weston_view_has_valid_buffer(ev)) {
-			drm_debug(b, "\t\t\t\t[view] not assigning view %p to plane "
+			/* A view with no buffer at all (e.g. kiosk-shell's
+			 * solid-colour background surface, created directly
+			 * via weston_solid_color_surface without a wl_buffer)
+			 * cannot go on a plane AND has nothing to render - it
+			 * is entirely invisible. In PLANES_ONLY mode
+			 * renderer_ok is false, so force_renderer=true here
+			 * would abort the whole state proposal (see the
+			 * '!ps && !renderer_ok' check below) and prevent real
+			 * client surfaces from being promoted to hardware
+			 * planes. Instead, skip the view silently: it
+			 * occupies no pixels and does not need to block plane
+			 * assignment for other views. */
+			drm_debug(b, "\t\t\t\t[view] ignoring view %p "
 			             "(no buffer available)\n", ev);
-			force_renderer = true;
+			pixman_region32_fini(&surface_overlap);
+			pixman_region32_fini(&clipped_view);
+			continue;
 		}
 
 		/* We can support this with the 'CRTC background colour' property,
